defmodule <%= @module %> do
  @moduledoc """
  Native Mob port of Mishka Chelekom's **headless Bar Chart** — rows of data
  drawn as bars against one shared scale, horizontally or as columns.

  A chart is a collection, and every app writes it by hand: the gutter is
  measured differently in each screen, one of the four forgets that the loudest
  bar is the scale, and the reading beside one bar drifts a few points from the
  reading beside the next. This draws the collection once — the scale in one
  place, the rhythm in one place, the tap in one place — and leaves every colour,
  size and word to the caller.

  ## The rows are data

  `rows` is a list, and each entry is either

    * a map — `%{label: "Action", value: 6, value_text: "6h", color: 0xFF4E9A73,
      value_font: "mono", id: "action", on_tap: :open_action, on_long_press:
      {pid, :peek}}` — with only `value` required, or
    * a tuple — `{"Action", 6}` or `{"Action", 6, 0xFF4E9A73}`, shorthand for
      the map above.

  The component never formats a number. `value` is the number the scale is
  computed from and `value_text` is the string a person reads — `6h`, `72%`,
  `3 of 5`. With `show_values` and no `value_text` the raw number is drawn,
  which is the one formatting this file does and it adds nothing to it.

  ## The scale is one scale

  Bars run from zero to `max`. Left unset, `max` is the loudest row, which is
  what a "where did it go" chart wants: four similar records stay four
  distinguishable bars instead of flattening against a round axis. A fixed
  `max` is what a progress-like chart wants, where 100 is the point of the
  chart and a full bar has to mean full.

  A row above `max` clamps to a full bar rather than overshooting its track, and
  a chart whose rows are all zero draws empty bars — no division by a zero
  range, and no `weight: 0.0`, which Compose refuses with a throw.

  ## Two orientations, one component

  `:horizontal` is the ranking — a label gutter, the bar, the reading. The
  gutter is **declared**, not measured: Mob reports no geometry back into
  `render/1`, so `label_width` is what keeps a column of bars starting at the
  same x. `nil` lets the label hug its own text, which is right for a single
  row and wrong for a chart, so pass a number when they must line up. The same
  holds for `value_width` at the other end.

  `:vertical` is the series — a row of columns on one baseline, values above,
  labels below. Each column's height comes from `height` and the row's fraction,
  so it is arithmetic rather than measurement and is the same on both platforms.
  There is no animation: a drawn bar changes between renders, it does not tween.

  ## Taps

  A row can be tapped and long-pressed. The handler goes through
  `<%= @namespace %>.Event.handler/2`, so the message carries the row:
  `{:tap, {tag, key}}` and `{:long_press, {tag, key}}`, where `key` is the row's
  `id` — its index when it has none. A row's own `on_tap` / `on_long_press`
  wins over the chart's, for a chart where one bar means something else.

  ## Selection is the caller's state

  `selected` names a row by that same key. The selected row is drawn in
  `selected_color` when one is given, and its reading is drawn even when
  `show_values` is false — so "tap a bar and see what it is" needs no extra
  design. The component holds no state: the screen sets `selected` on the event
  it asked for, and the chart redraws.

  ## A banded scale, or a ramp

  `color_scale` colours a bar by **where it falls** instead of by a colour the
  row carries: `color_scale: [{0.0, 0xFFB3564E}, {0.3, 0xFF5B7CA8}, {1.0,
  0xFF8A8177}]` reads "under 30% is red, under 100% is blue, a full bar is
  grey". `scale_mode` decides what happens *between* two stops:

    * `:steps` (the default) is strict — a bar takes the colour of the last stop
      at or below it, and a bar under the first stop takes the first stop's
      colour, because a banded scale has no colour for "less than red";
    * `:fade` blends the two surrounding colours linearly, channel by channel,
      so the scale is a continuous ramp.

  Fading needs **ARGB integers**. A colour token is resolved by the renderer and
  cannot be mixed in Elixir, so a token under `:fade` is used as given at the
  stop below it. A row's own `color` always wins over the scale, and so does
  `selected_color` — a caller highlighting one bar should not lose that to a
  band.

  ## What it does not do

  No axes, no gridlines, no legend, no tooltip and no animation. Each of those
  is a layout of its own — a legend is a wrap, an axis is measured text — and a
  bar chart that needs them is a page rather than a component. `limit` with
  `more_text` covers the one thing every real list needs: a cap with a count.

  ## Props

  | Prop | Values | Default | Meaning |
  |------|--------|---------|---------|
  | `rows` | list of maps / tuples | `[]` | One entry per bar, in reading order. |
  | `orientation` | `:horizontal` `:vertical` | `:horizontal` | Ranking rows, or columns on a baseline. |
  | `max` | number / `nil` | loudest row | The value a full bar means. |
  | `bar_size` | number / `nil` | `6` horizontal; fills the slot vertically | Bar thickness, or column width. |
  | `gap` | number | `10` | Space between rows, or between columns. |
  | `corner_radius` | number | `3` | Rounding on the bar and its track. |
  | `color` | color token / ARGB int | `:primary` | The default fill; a row's own wins. |
  | `color_scale` | list of `{at, color}` | `nil` | Colours by fraction when a row names none. |
  | `scale_mode` | `:steps` `:fade` | `:steps` | Bands, or a blend between two stops. |
  | `track_color` | color token / ARGB int | `:transparent` | The groove behind each bar. |
  | `selected` | term / `nil` | `nil` | The key of the selected row. |
  | `selected_color` | color token / ARGB int | `nil` | The selected row's fill, when given. |
  | `selected_value_color` | color token / ARGB int | `value_color` | The selected row's reading ink. |
  | `show_values` | boolean | `false` | Draw each row's reading. |
  | `value_width` | number / `nil` | `nil` | A declared width for the reading, so the tracks end at one x. |
  | `value_size` | number | `12` | The reading's size (11 as a column's). |
  | `value_color` | color token / ARGB int | `:muted` | The reading's ink. |
  | `value_weight` | weight | unset | The reading's weight. |
  | `value_font` | string | unset | The reading's face. |
  | `value_gap` | number | `8` horizontal, `3` vertical | Between a bar and its reading, or a column's reading and its top. |
  | `label_width` | number / `nil` | `84` | The gutter, horizontal only; `nil` hugs. |
  | `label_size` | number | `12.5` | The label's size (11 as a column's). |
  | `label_color` | color token / ARGB int | `:on_surface` | The label's ink. |
  | `label_weight` | weight | unset | The label's weight. |
  | `label_font` | string | unset | The label's face. |
  | `label_gap` | number | `12` | Between the gutter and the bar. |
  | `height` | number | `120` | The plot height, vertical only. |
  | `on_tap` | tag / `{pid, tag}` | `nil` | Tapping any bar, with the row's key. |
  | `on_long_press` | tag / `{pid, tag}` | `nil` | Pressing any bar, with the row's key. |
  | `limit` | integer / `nil` | `nil` | Draw only the first N rows. |
  | `more_text` | string | `nil` | Drawn under the plot when rows were cut. |
  | `more_size` | number | `11` | The tail's size. |
  | `more_color` | color token / ARGB int | `:muted` | The tail's ink. |
  | `id` | string | unset | TestTag on the chart; rows are `<id>-<key>` unless they carry their own. |

  Children are ignored; the chart is data.

  **Documentation:** https://mishka.tools/chelekom/docs/mob/bar-chart
  """

  import Mob.Sigil

  alias <%= @namespace %>.Event
  alias <%= @namespace %>.<%= @module_prefix_camel %>Progress

  @doc "Composite expander (`<<%= @module_prefix_camel %>BarChart />`). Delegates to `bar_chart/1`."
  @spec expand(map(), [map()], map()) :: map()
  def expand(props, _children, _ctx), do: <%= @component_prefix %>bar_chart(props)

  @doc """
  The chart.

      <%= @component_prefix %>bar_chart(rows: [%{label: "Action", value: 6, value_text: "6h"}])
      <%= @component_prefix %>bar_chart(rows: [{"Action", 6}, {"Adventure", 5}], orientation: :vertical)
  """
  @spec <%= @component_prefix %>bar_chart(map() | keyword()) :: map()
  def <%= @component_prefix %>bar_chart(props \\ %{}) do
    props = Map.new(props)
    rows = rows(props)
    {shown, hidden} = capped(rows, Map.get(props, :limit))
    max = scale_max(props, rows)

    plot =
      case setting(props, :orientation, :horizontal) do
        :vertical -> columns(shown, props, max)
        _horizontal -> bars(shown, props, max)
      end

    ~MOB"""
    <Column fill_width={true}>
      {plot}
      {tail(hidden, props)}
    </Column>
    """
    |> put_id(Map.get(props, :id))
  end

  @doc """
  The fraction a row's value occupies on the scale, clamped to `0.0..1.0`.

      iex> <%= @namespace %>.<%= @module_prefix_camel %>BarChart.fraction(5, 10)
      0.5
      iex> <%= @namespace %>.<%= @module_prefix_camel %>BarChart.fraction(14, 10)
      1.0
      iex> <%= @namespace %>.<%= @module_prefix_camel %>BarChart.fraction(5, 0)
      0.0
  """
  @spec fraction(number() | nil, number() | nil) :: float()
  def fraction(_value, max) when not is_number(max) or max <= 0, do: 0.0

  def fraction(value, max) when is_number(value) do
    (value / max) |> max(0.0) |> min(1.0) |> Kernel.*(1.0)
  end

  def fraction(_value, _max), do: 0.0

  @doc """
  The colour a fraction takes on a stop scale.

  `stops` is a list of `{at, color}` with `at` in `0.0..1.0`. Under `:steps` a
  fraction takes the colour of the last stop at or below it (a fraction under
  the first stop takes the first stop's colour), which is a banded scale. Under
  `:fade` the two surrounding colours are blended linearly, channel by channel,
  which is a continuous ramp.

  Fading needs **ARGB integers**: a colour token is resolved by the renderer and
  cannot be mixed here, so a token under `:fade` is used as given at the stop
  below it.

      iex> <%= @namespace %>.<%= @module_prefix_camel %>BarChart.scale_color([{0.0, 0xFFFF0000}, {0.3, 0xFF0000FF}], 0.2)
      0xFFFF0000
      iex> <%= @namespace %>.<%= @module_prefix_camel %>BarChart.scale_color([{0.0, 0xFFFF0000}, {0.3, 0xFF0000FF}], 0.5)
      0xFF0000FF
      iex> <%= @namespace %>.<%= @module_prefix_camel %>BarChart.scale_color([{0.0, 0xFF000000}, {1.0, 0xFFFFFFFF}], 0.5, :fade)
      0xFF808080
  """
  @spec scale_color([{number(), term()}], number(), :steps | :fade) :: term()
  def scale_color([_single] = stops, _fraction, _mode), do: elem(hd(stops), 1)

  def scale_color(stops, fraction, mode) do
    stops = Enum.sort_by(stops, &elem(&1, 0))

    case mode do
      :fade -> fade_at(stops, fraction)
      _steps -> step_at(stops, fraction)
    end
  end

  defp step_at([{_at, color}], _fraction), do: color

  defp step_at([{_at, color}, {next_at, next_color} | rest], fraction) do
    if fraction >= next_at, do: step_at([{next_at, next_color} | rest], fraction), else: color
  end

  # Below the first stop is the first stop's colour: a banded scale has no
  # colour for "less than red" and inventing one here would surprise the caller.
  defp step_at([{_at, color} | _rest], _fraction), do: color

  defp fade_at([{_at, color}], _fraction), do: color

  defp fade_at([{at, color}, {next_at, next_color} | rest], fraction) do
    cond do
      fraction <= at -> color
      fraction < next_at -> blend(color, next_color, (fraction - at) / (next_at - at))
      true -> fade_at([{next_at, next_color} | rest], fraction)
    end
  end

  defp blend(from, to, t) when is_integer(from) and is_integer(to) do
    import Bitwise

    mix = fn a, b -> round(a + (b - a) * t) end

    a = mix.(from >>> 24 &&& 0xFF, to >>> 24 &&& 0xFF)
    r = mix.(from >>> 16 &&& 0xFF, to >>> 16 &&& 0xFF)
    g = mix.(from >>> 8 &&& 0xFF, to >>> 8 &&& 0xFF)
    b = mix.(from &&& 0xFF, to &&& 0xFF)

    a <<< 24 ||| r <<< 16 ||| g <<< 8 ||| b
  end

  defp blend(from, _to, _t), do: from

  # ── Rows ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  defp rows(props) do
    props
    |> Map.get(:rows, [])
    |> Enum.with_index()
    |> Enum.map(fn {row, index} -> row(row, index) end)
  end

  defp row(%{} = row, index) do
    %{
      key: Map.get(row, :id) || index,
      label: Map.get(row, :label),
      value: Map.get(row, :value) || 0,
      value_text: Map.get(row, :value_text),
      value_font: Map.get(row, :value_font),
      color: Map.get(row, :color),
      on_tap: Map.get(row, :on_tap),
      on_long_press: Map.get(row, :on_long_press)
    }
  end

  defp row({label, value}, index) when is_binary(label) do
    row(%{label: label, value: value}, index)
  end

  defp row({label, value, color}, index) when is_binary(label) do
    row(%{label: label, value: value, color: color}, index)
  end

  defp row(_none, index), do: row(%{}, index)

  defp capped(rows, limit) when is_integer(limit) and limit >= 0 do
    {Enum.take(rows, limit), max(length(rows) - limit, 0)}
  end

  defp capped(rows, _limit), do: {rows, 0}

  defp scale_max(props, rows) do
    case Map.get(props, :max) do
      number when is_number(number) and number > 0 -> number
      _none -> rows |> Enum.map(& &1.value) |> Enum.max(fn -> 0 end) |> max(0)
    end
  end

  # ── Horizontal ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  defp bars(rows, props, max) do
    gap = spacer(setting(props, :gap, 10))

    nodes =
      rows
      |> Enum.with_index()
      |> Enum.map(fn {row, _index} -> bar(row, props, max) end)
      |> Enum.intersperse(gap)

    assigns = %{nodes: nodes}

    ~MOB"""
    <Column fill_width={true}>
      {@nodes}
    </Column>
    """
  end

  defp bar(row, props, max) do
    assigns = %{
      label: label_node(row, props),
      gap: gap_node(setting(props, :label_gap, 12)),
      bar: progress(row, props, max),
      value: value_node(row, props),
      tap: handler(Map.get(row, :on_tap) || Map.get(props, :on_tap), row.key),
      hold: handler(Map.get(row, :on_long_press) || Map.get(props, :on_long_press), row.key),
      tag: row_tag(props, row)
    }

    ~MOB"""
    <Row fill_width={true} align="center" on_tap={@tap} on_long_press={@hold} id={@tag}>
      {@label}
      {@gap}
      <Box weight={1.0}>
        {@bar}
      </Box>
      {@value}
    </Row>
    """
    |> drop_unset(:id, assigns.tag)
    |> drop_unset(:on_tap, assigns.tap)
    |> drop_unset(:on_long_press, assigns.hold)
  end

  defp label_node(%{label: nil}, _props), do: []

  defp label_node(%{label: label}, props) do
    assigns = %{
      label: label,
      size: setting(props, :label_size, 12.5),
      color: setting(props, :label_color, :on_surface),
      weight: Map.get(props, :label_weight),
      font: Map.get(props, :label_font),
      width: Map.get(props, :label_width)
    }

    text =
      ~MOB"""
      <Text
        text={@label}
        text_size={@size}
        text_color={@color}
        font_weight={@weight}
        font_family={@font}
        max_lines={1}
      />
      """
      |> drop_unset(:font_family, assigns.font)

    width_box(text, assigns.width)
  end

  defp progress(row, props, max) do
    <%= @module_prefix_camel %>Progress.<%= @component_prefix %>progress(%{
      value: fraction(row.value, max),
      max: 1,
      render: :box,
      height: setting(props, :bar_size, 6),
      corner_radius: setting(props, :corner_radius, 3),
      color: fill(row, props, max),
      track_color: setting(props, :track_color, :transparent)
    })
  end

  # The reading sits after the track, at the row's end, and a declared
  # `value_width` is what keeps every track ending at the same x.
  defp value_node(row, props) do
    if shown_value?(row, props) do
      assigns = %{
        text: reading(row),
        size: setting(props, :value_size, 12),
        color: value_ink(row, props),
        weight: Map.get(props, :value_weight),
        font: row.value_font || Map.get(props, :value_font),
        width: Map.get(props, :value_width)
      }

      text =
        ~MOB"""
        <Text
          text={@text}
          text_size={@size}
          text_color={@color}
          font_weight={@weight}
          font_family={@font}
          text_align="right"
          max_lines={1}
        />
        """
        |> drop_unset(:font_family, assigns.font)

      [gap_node(setting(props, :value_gap, 8)), width_box(text, assigns.width)]
    else
      []
    end
  end

  defp width_box(text, nil), do: text

  defp width_box(text, width) do
    assigns = %{width: width, text: text}

    ~MOB"""
    <Column width={@width}>
      {@text}
    </Column>
    """
  end

  # ── Vertical ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  defp columns(rows, props, max) do
    gap = spacer(setting(props, :gap, 10))

    nodes =
      rows
      |> Enum.with_index()
      |> Enum.map(fn {row, _index} -> column(row, props, max) end)
      |> Enum.intersperse(gap)

    assigns = %{nodes: nodes}

    ~MOB"""
    <Row fill_width={true} align="bottom">
      {@nodes}
    </Row>
    """
  end

  defp column(row, props, max) do
    assigns = %{
      value: column_value(row, props),
      plot: column_plot(row, props, max),
      label: column_label(row, props),
      tap: handler(Map.get(row, :on_tap) || Map.get(props, :on_tap), row.key),
      hold: handler(Map.get(row, :on_long_press) || Map.get(props, :on_long_press), row.key),
      tag: row_tag(props, row)
    }

    ~MOB"""
    <Column weight={1.0} align="center" on_tap={@tap} on_long_press={@hold} id={@tag}>
      {@value}
      {@plot}
      {@label}
    </Column>
    """
    |> drop_unset(:id, assigns.tag)
    |> drop_unset(:on_tap, assigns.tap)
    |> drop_unset(:on_long_press, assigns.hold)
  end

  defp column_value(row, props) do
    if shown_value?(row, props) do
      assigns = %{
        text: reading(row),
        size: setting(props, :value_size, 11),
        color: value_ink(row, props),
        weight: Map.get(props, :value_weight),
        font: row.value_font || Map.get(props, :value_font)
      }

      ~MOB"""
      <Text
        text={@text}
        text_size={@size}
        text_color={@color}
        font_weight={@weight}
        font_family={@font}
        text_align="center"
        max_lines={1}
      />
      """
      |> drop_unset(:font_family, assigns.font)
      |> then(&[&1, gap_node(setting(props, :value_gap, 3))])
    else
      []
    end
  end

  # An empty part is a Spacer, a filled part a Box under it, so the fill sits on
  # the baseline without a `justify` the bridge does not have.
  defp column_plot(row, props, max) do
    height = setting(props, :height, 120)
    filled = round(height * fraction(row.value, max))

    assigns = %{
      height: height,
      empty: max(height - filled, 0),
      fill: filled,
      color: fill(row, props, max),
      track: setting(props, :track_color, :transparent),
      radius: setting(props, :corner_radius, 3),
      width: Map.get(props, :bar_size)
    }

    empty = gap_node(assigns.empty)

    fill =
      if filled > 0 do
        ~MOB"""
        <Box fill_width={true} height={@fill} background={@color} corner_radius={@radius} />
        """
      else
        []
      end

    ~MOB"""
    <Column
      fill_width={@width == nil}
      width={@width}
      height={@height}
      background={@track}
      corner_radius={@radius}
    >
      {empty}
      {fill}
    </Column>
    """
    |> drop_unset(:width, assigns.width)
  end

  defp column_label(%{label: nil}, _props), do: []

  defp column_label(%{label: label}, props) do
    assigns = %{
      label: label,
      size: setting(props, :label_size, 11),
      color: setting(props, :label_color, :on_surface),
      weight: Map.get(props, :label_weight),
      font: Map.get(props, :label_font)
    }

    ~MOB"""
    <Column fill_width={true} align="center">
      <Spacer size={6} />
      <Text
        text={@label}
        text_size={@size}
        text_color={@color}
        font_weight={@weight}
        font_family={@font}
        text_align="center"
        max_lines={1}
      />
    </Column>
    """
    |> drop_unset(:font_family, assigns.font)
  end

  # ── Shared ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  defp shown_value?(row, props) do
    selected?(row, props) or Map.get(props, :show_values, false)
  end

  defp reading(row), do: row.value_text || to_string(row.value)

  defp value_ink(row, props) do
    if selected?(row, props) do
      setting(props, :selected_value_color, setting(props, :value_color, :muted))
    else
      setting(props, :value_color, :muted)
    end
  end

  defp fill(row, props, max) do
    cond do
      selected?(row, props) and Map.get(props, :selected_color) ->
        Map.get(props, :selected_color)

      row.color ->
        row.color

      scale = Map.get(props, :color_scale) ->
        scale_color(
          scale,
          fraction(row.value, max),
          Map.get(props, :scale_mode, :steps)
        )

      true ->
        setting(props, :color, :primary)
    end
  end

  defp selected?(row, props) do
    case Map.get(props, :selected) do
      nil -> false
      key -> key == row.key
    end
  end

  defp tail(0, _props), do: []

  defp tail(_hidden, props) do
    case Map.get(props, :more_text) do
      nil ->
        []

      text ->
        assigns = %{
          text: text,
          size: setting(props, :more_size, 11),
          color: setting(props, :more_color, :muted)
        }

        ~MOB"""
        <Column fill_width={true}>
          <Spacer size={8} />
          <Text text={@text} text_size={@size} text_color={@color} max_lines={1} />
        </Column>
        """
    end
  end

  defp row_tag(props, row) do
    case Map.get(props, :id) do
      nil -> nil
      id -> "#{id}-#{row.key}"
    end
  end

  defp handler(nil, _key), do: nil
  defp handler(tag, key), do: Event.handler(tag, key)

  defp gap_node(size) when is_number(size) and size > 0, do: spacer(size)
  defp gap_node(_size), do: []

  defp spacer(size) do
    assigns = %{size: size}
    ~MOB"<Spacer size={@size} />"
  end

  # A prop left unset is omitted rather than sent as nil: a present-but-nil
  # `font_family` makes the bridge resolve the fallback face, which draws the
  # string at a different weight from the same string in a screen's own Text.
  defp drop_unset(node, _key, value) when not is_nil(value), do: node
  defp drop_unset(node, key, _value), do: %{node | props: Map.delete(node.props, key)}

  defp setting(props, key, default), do: Map.get(props, key) || default

  defp put_id(node, nil), do: node
  defp put_id(node, id), do: %{node | props: Map.put(node.props, :id, id)}
end
